        <ArticleTitle>Cardiovascular outcomes with GLP-1 receptor agonists in type 2 diabetes: a systematic review.</ArticleTitle>
        <Pagination>
          <MedlinePgn>1010-1018</MedlinePgn>
        </Pagination>
        <Abstract>
          <AbstractText Label="BACKGROUND" NlmCategory="BACKGROUND">GLP-1 receptor agonists reduce major adverse cardiovascular events in patients with type 2 diabetes.</AbstractText>
          <AbstractText Label="METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">We performed a systematic review of randomized controlled trials.</AbstractText>
          <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">Across 12 trials, the pooled hazard ratio was 0.86.</AbstractText>
          <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSIONS" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">GLP-1 receptor agonists confer significant cardiovascular benefit.</AbstractText>
        </Abstract>
