        <ArticleTitle>Semaglutide in patients with obesity and heart failure with preserved ejection fraction.</ArticleTitle>
        <Pagination>
          <MedlinePgn>1989-2001</MedlinePgn>
        </Pagination>
        <Abstract>
          <AbstractText Label="BACKGROUND" NlmCategory="BACKGROUND">Semaglutide improved symptoms and physical function in patients with obesity and heart failure with preserved ejection fraction.</AbstractText>
          <AbstractText Label="METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">In this double-blind trial, we randomly assigned 529 patients to receive semaglutide or placebo.</AbstractText>
          <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">The primary end point was the change in the Kansas City Cardiomyopathy Questionnaire clinical summary score.</AbstractText>
          <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSIONS" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Semaglutide led to a larger reduction in symptoms and physical limitations.</AbstractText>
        </Abstract>
